    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d260">

                <pb facs="0283" n="271" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg271"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">874.00/7–2545: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the United States Representative in Bulgaria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Barnes</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-27T17:00:00-04:00">July 27, 1945—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>222. Urtel 383, July 25. In considering further action in Dimitrov case Dept will
                    appreciate your present views<anchor n="13" xml:id="d260-f1"/> whether we could
                    accept any, and if so what, arrangements and assurances by Bulgarian Govt as
                    providing adequate protection for Dimitrov should he remain in the country.
                    Please ascertain Dimitrov’s own attitude toward any such arrangements and
                    assurances.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d260-f1" n="13" xml:id="d260-f1-content">
                <p>For reply, see telegram 481, August 28, 9 a.m., from Sofia, <ref target="#pg313"
                        >p. 313</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
